<title>USA: Conn. sees casinos exceeding revenue 1997 goals.</title>
<headline>Conn. sees casinos exceeding revenue 1997 goals.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Connecticut Division of Special Revenue, which oversees gaming in the state, said it expects to get over $200 million from slot machine in 1997, around $4 million more than first anticipated.</p>
<p>Connecticut gets 25 percent of the take from slots at both the Foxwoods and Mohegan Sun casinos.</p>
<p>The new Mohegan Sun was projected to hand over about $58 million to the state, while Foxwoods, which has 2,000 more slots than the Mohegan Sun, was estimated to contribute around $142 million dollars.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
